  this runner. Identical outcome to siblings 0006 / 0007 / 0008 / 0009 / 0010 / 0011 / 0012 / 0013
  (all -> EXIT=1 / STATUS=BLOCKED). The prompt's capability clause is explicit: "requires WinUI 3 (Windows App
  SDK 1.6+) + .NET 10 ... If unavailable on the runner -> STATUS=BLOCKED with API evidence." WinUI 3 / .NET 10
  ARE present (BUILD_EXIT=0 proves the WinUI view compiles + links; the 1772 headless tests run on net10.0). The
  only absent capability is the GUI-automation runner.

=== ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA (surface contribution - all met within the available capability) ===
  [x] Surface renders all web-source states: loading (full-area skeleton), loaded (radial state-of-health gauge
      tinted by the web scoreColor threshold [>=80 green / >=50 amber / else red] + integer score caption +
      the six stat tiles Cycles / Charge Depth% / Discharge% / DC Fast% / Temp Score(/100) / Habits(/100) when
      standard), compact (gauge only, no title/stats; web isCompact = cols<=1), empty ("No battery health
      data"), error (TsQueryError + retry), stale (gauge + freshness chip), offline (gauge + offline chip).
      Built + headless per-state tested.
